# Starforge Email Manager — modular ownership

Any Starforge module that sends product email **must** use `product:email-manager`. Do not call `getMailer()` / `sendMail()` from consumer packs (Forms, Events, Payments, …). Auth recovery may stay on Core Mailer until it is moved onto triggers. Email Manager is a **base module**; the Mailer port stays Core (`sf-architecture.mdc`).

## Source of truth

| Concern | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| Trigger → rule → template → send | **`product:email-manager`** — `emitEmailTrigger` |
| Paced bulk send (caller-supplied audience) | **`product:email-manager`** — `enqueueEmailBroadcast` |
| Campaign (label + template + pasted recipients) | **`product:email-manager`** — Send copies the saved paste into `enqueueEmailBroadcast` (`sourceKey` `email-campaign:<id>`); status moves draft → sending → sent/cancelled/failed from the broadcast row; counts are the broadcast counters. List edit expands on `/admin/email/campaigns` (clickable label; half-width mosaic cards). The expand lists broadcast recipient rows (address, status, error), filtered and capped at 200. Open/click tracking and a durable subscriber list stay out. |
| Transport / From / provider secrets | **Core Mailer** + Site Chrome / env |
| Template HTML editing | **`product:rich-editor`** (email preset) + Media picker |
| Durable subscriber lists / segments | **`product:campaigns`** (later) — not this pack |

Transactional emits stay immediate (one audience per trigger). Hundreds of recipients go through the broadcast queue (batch + gap). Pace rules live under `/admin/email/broadcasts`. Campaign Send uses that same pipe; Pause / Resume / Cancel stay on the broadcasts admin.

## Do

- Emit named triggers with `emitEmailTrigger` from `@/modules/email-manager/api.server`.
- Queue bulk audiences with `enqueueEmailBroadcast` (template id + recipient rows + `sourceKey`).
- Soft-skip when Email Manager is off or no rule matches.
- Deep-link admins to `/admin/email` for copy and pace — do not rebuild SMTP or template UIs in the consumer.

## Don’t

- Call `getMailer()` from Events, Forms, Payments, or other product packs for product mail.
- Loop `mailer.send` in a consumer for a registrant / order list.
- Treat Email Manager as a mailing-list product — durable lists/segments are `product:campaigns`. Light pasted-recipient campaigns live here.
- Seed organizer-notify / reminder / cancellation templates in a pass that only needs paced registrant mail (leave existing seeds alone).
- Export campaign helpers on `api` / `api.server`.

## Quick check

If the message fires because something already happened (registered, paid, form submitted) → trigger. If an admin picks a template and a list of rows → `enqueueEmailBroadcast`. If they save a draft name + template + paste and hit Send → Email Manager campaign → one paced broadcast (`email-campaign:<id>`), not `product:campaigns`.
